\title "Travis picking"
\subtitle "Guitar (standard tuning), G major chord shape"
\copyright "Pattern under MIT or Apache-2.0."
\tempo 80
\tuning E4 B3 G3 D3 A2 E2
.
// Merle Travis / Chet Atkins fingerstyle pattern. The thumb keeps
// a steady alternating bass between the root (low G, string 6
// fret 3) and the 5th (open D, string 4), playing on every beat.
// The index + middle fingers fill the off-beats with notes from
// the chord's upper strings — same open G shape as the boom-chick
// pattern, so muscle memory transfers.
//
// Hold open G: 3 2 0 0 0 3. The drill is purely about the
// thumb-fills-fingers timing.
//
//   col 0  thumb → bass G    (3.6)
//   col 1  index → string 3  (open G3)
//   col 2  thumb → bass D    (0.4)
//   col 3  middle → string 1 (3.1, high G)
//   col 4  thumb → bass G
//   col 5  index → string 3
//   col 6  thumb → bass D
//   col 7  middle → string 1
:8 3.6 0.3 0.4 3.1 3.6 0.3 0.4 3.1 |
:8 3.6 0.3 0.4 3.1 3.6 0.3 0.4 3.1 |
